<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bohemond I of Antioch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1054–1111</span> · Also known as Bohemond of Taranto</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bohemond I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> was a Norman leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>, eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-guiscard">Robert Guiscard</a>. Given Taranto in 1088, he joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> and in 1098 secured Antioch for himself, founding the Principality of Antioch. Captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danishmendids">Danishmendids</a> in 1100 and ransomed in 1103, he later attacked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> but had to accept the Treaty of Devol in 1108.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bohemond-i-of-antioch.jpg" alt="Bohemond I of Antioch" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maître de Fauvel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bohemond_I_of_Antioch_lib.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
